{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252{\fonttbl{\f0\froman Calibri;}{\f1\froman Source Sans Pro;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue255;}{\stylesheet {\snext0 Normal;}}\fet0\ftnbj\uc1 {\footer Page \chpgn .  Exported from {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.logos.com/"}{\fldrslt\ul\cf1 Logos Bible Study}}, 7:07\u8239?AM March 25, 2026.}\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\sb160\sa160 {\b The Future!}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\fs52 {\b Reality Check}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 Goal: Validate that their anxiety isn't "wrong," it\rquote s a response to a real environment.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 1. {\b Question:} "If you look at the news or think about graduation, what is the one thing that feels like it\rquote s 'shaking' the most right now?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 2. {\b Question:} "Is it possible to have 100% control over your life? If not, what percentage do you think we actually have?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 3. {\b Question:} \ldblquote If you could guarantee one specific thing about your life 10 years from now, would that eliminate all your fear, or just change it?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 4. {\b The "Past Evidence" File:} "Even if you're only 15 or 17, where has God already shown up for you? How can that 'history' help you trust Him with your college major?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Transition:} "I felt that loss of control when I faced a layoff. I realized adults don't have it all figured out; we just have bigger stakes. But I found that while the 'shaking' is real, the Anchor is more real."}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\fs52 {\b THE Foundation} {\b PROMISE: The Hand in the Dark: }({\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://ref.ly/Is41.10-13"}{\fldrslt\ul\cf1 Isaiah 41:10\endash 13}})}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Goal:} Establish that God is a Person who is present in history and personal life.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 5. {\b Opening Question:} \rdblquote When you\rquote re in a dark room, do you need a lecture on how light works, or someone to just come in and sit with you?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb40\sa40 {\b\fs36 {\b Scripture: }{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://ref.ly/Is41.10-13"}{\fldrslt\ul\cf1 Isaiah 41:10\endash 13}}  The Old Testament Narrative: \line Theme: God as the Steadying Hand in World Turmoil }\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Notes:} Isaiah was writing to a people facing national upheaval, war, and displacement\emdash very similar to the "world turmoil" your teens are sensing.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Key Verse:} {\i "For I, the Lord your God, hold your right hand; it is I who say to you, 'Fear not, I am the one who helps you.'" (v. 13)}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Study Focus:} Use the imagery of the "right hand." In your story about the layoff, you didn't know where the path was going, but you knew {\i who} was holding your hand. This helps teens shift their focus from the scary "thing" (the news, a school shooting threat, college apps) to the person of God.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 6. {\b Question:} "In verse 13, God says He 'holds your right hand.' If someone is holding your hand, how close do they have to be? Can they hold your hand from across the room or through a screen?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 7. {\b Question:} "Notice God says, 'I will help you.' Does that mean the problem disappears, or that He\rquote s in the middle of it with you?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Truth:} You aren't being guided by a map; you\rquote re being guided by a {\b Person}.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Image:} God isn't shouting directions from a distance. He is "holding your right hand."}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Reflection:} If God is holding your hand right now, does the "where" of your future matter as much as the "who" you are with?}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Bridge Statement:} "This promise wasn't just for people 3,000 years ago. Because of Jesus, we are part of this same family. This is the 'Warranty' we carry into the future."}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\fs52 {\b The Gospel Anchor} ({\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://ref.ly/Mt6.25-34"}{\fldrslt\ul\cf1 Matthew 6:25\endash 34}})}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 Goal: See how Jesus expands that promise into the "Small Stuff" and "Big Stuff."}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 8. "How is talking to a friend who has 'been there' different from reading a manual on how to be happy?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb40\sa40 {\b\fs36 {\b Scripture:} {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://ref.ly/Mt6.25-34"}{\fldrslt\ul\cf1 {\i Matthew 6:25\endash 34}}}{\i  }}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Theme: Prioritizing the Kingdom over the "What-Ifs"}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Notes: }This is the quintessential text for anxiety because Jesus addresses the most basic human fears (food, clothing, longevity) and scales them up to the "unknowns" of tomorrow.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Key Verse:} {\i "Therefore do not be anxious about tomorrow, for tomorrow will be anxious for itself. Sufficient for the day is its own trouble." (v. 34)}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Study Focus:} Help the teens see that God doesn't promise a blueprint of their entire 20s or 30s. Instead, He promises presence for {\i today}. The "exercise" here is the discipline of presence\emdash focusing on being faithful in high school right now rather than solving a career crisis that is years away.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 9. {\b Question:} "Jesus talks about birds and flowers. Why do you think He uses nature to talk to people who are worried about their lives and their futures?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 10. {\b Question:} "Verse 34 says 'tomorrow will be anxious for itself.' Is that a relief to hear, or does it make you more nervous? Why?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 11. {\b Question:} "Jesus says to 'Seek first the Kingdom.' If you\rquote re worried about a math test or a school shooting, what does 'seeking the Kingdom' look like in that exact moment?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Truth:} Anxiety is usually "living in a future that hasn't happened yet."}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Image:} The birds and the lilies don\rquote t "hustle" for their worth. They simply exist in God's care.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Reflection:} What is one "Tomorrow Problem" you can hand back to Jesus so you can focus on being faithful {\b today}?}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Bridge Statement:} "Jesus is making the Isaiah promise concrete. He\rquote s saying: 'I am the God who holds your hand, and I\rquote m also the God who knows you need a career and a future.'"}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\fs52 {\b The Prayer of Presence} (Psalm 46:1\endash 3, 10)}\par \pard\sb40\sa40 {\b\fs36 {\b THE PRACTICE: The Power of Being Still}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\i Goal: Give them a practical "Exercise" to use when the world feels loud.}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 12.  {\b Opening Question:} \ldblquote Think of your best friend. Did that friendship happen because of one big event, or a thousand small, boring moments?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Scripture:} {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://ref.ly/Ps46.1-3"}{\fldrslt\ul\cf1 {\i Psalm 46:1\endash 3}}}{\i , }{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://ref.ly/Ps46.10"}{\fldrslt\ul\cf1 {\i 10}}}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Theme: Finding a Fortress in a Shaking World}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Notes:} This Psalm is unique because it acknowledges that the earth might literally "give way" and the "mountains move into the heart of the sea." It doesn't minimize the chaos of the world; it places God above it.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Key Verse:} {\i "Be still, and know that I am God. I will be exalted among the nations, I will be exalted in the earth!" (v. 10)}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b Study Focus:} The Hebrew word for "be still" ({\i raphah}) can also mean "let go" or "surrender." This ties directly into your personal example. The struggle isn't just "not worrying"; it's the active spiritual exercise of "letting go" of the need to control the outcome and "resting" in God\rquote s sovereignty.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 13. {\b Question:} "The Psalm describes the earth 'giving way' and mountains falling into the sea. When you hear about wars or divisions in the world, does it feel like the mountains are falling?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 14. {\b Question:} "Verse 10 says 'Be still.' In a world that tells you to 'hustle' or 'worry' to get ahead, why is being still so difficult? Is it a passive thing or an active choice?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Truth:} Faith is an {\b exercise}. We don't just "have" it; we "do" it.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Image:} A Fortress. When the earth shakes, the Fortress doesn't move.}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Exercise:} {\i Selah} (Pause). Take 60 seconds of silence. Use the phrase: {\i "Be still, and know that I am God."}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b The Bridge Statement:} "This isn't just a poem; it's a practice. When I was looking for a job, I had to 'be still' and remember that God is God, and I am not. That is where the peace comes from\emdash knowing the Person who is in charge."}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\fs52 The Takeaway}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\i Goal: Commit to one "Exercise of Faith."}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 15. {\b Question:} Do you already have a practice that you find helpful for reminding yourself of God\rquote s promises when tough times strike, or fear and anxiety flood your emotions?}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 16. {\b Final Question:} "This week, when that 'shaking' feeling starts in your chest\emdash whether it's about a college app or a news headline\emdash which of these three images do you want to grab onto: The Hand (Isaiah), The Bird (Matthew), or The Fortress (Psalm)?"}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb40\sa40 {\b\fs36 {\b Why Christianity is Different}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 We don't just follow a philosophy or a set of "good vibes." We have a relationship with {\b Jesus Christ}\emdash God incarnate. Through the {\b Holy Spirit}, He is literally {\i with you} in the hallway, the classroom, and the quiet of your room. He isn't just watching you; He is walking with you.}\par \pard\sb40\sa40 {\b\fs36 {\b My "Evidence" File}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\i Adults don't have all the answers, but we have "History." Think of one time in the past when things felt scary, but God showed up or carried you through. Write it here to remind yourself that He is faithful:}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 {\b [ ]}}\par \pard\sb40\sa40 {\b\fs36 {\b This Week\rquote s Challenge:}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 When the "shaking" starts\emdash when you feel that knot of anxiety about school, the news, or your family\emdash stop for 10 seconds. Visualize God holding your right hand ({\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://ref.ly/Is41.13"}{\fldrslt\ul\cf1 Isaiah 41:13}}) and say: {\b "Lord, I don't know the future, but I know You."}}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\fs52 Question Corral}\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 17. What weakness that you confront daily can remind you to rely on God as your source of strength?}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 18. What does it mean when the Lord says, 'Fear not, for I am with you'? How does this relate to our everyday lives?}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 19. How do you see God demonstrating His strength and help in your life or the lives of those around you?}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 20. In what ways do you think God\rquote s assurance of 'upholding' and 'strengthening' us impacts our experience of fear or anxiety?}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 21. What action steps can you take this week to lean into God's strength, especially when facing challenges?}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 22. How can prayer play a role in helping us internalize the reassurance found in this passage?}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 23. What are some practical ways you can remind yourself of God's strength when you feel overwhelmed?}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 24. How can scripture play a role in helping us internalize the reassurance found in this passage?}\par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard \par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 }\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 }\par \pard\sb160\sa160 {\f1\fs24 }\par }